%I A397910 #13 Oct 14 2026 20:18:39
%S A397910 4691,176777,1409533,23185159,84474667,920765957,5075610989,
%T A397910 17393031977,189499828967,466911439271,2378827903247,13946348081951,
%U A397910 60934830657541,129555248013179,1138383441262829,3088372227674287,10787862040659943,38708026184211401
%N A397910 Smallest prime p such that 1 + (sum of primes <= p) >= exp(gamma(n)), where gamma(n) is the imaginary part of the n-th nontrivial zero of the Riemann zeta function.
%C A397910 Let S(x) = 1 + Sum_{p <= x} p. Then a(n) is the first prime at which log(S(p)) reaches gamma(n).
%C A397910 The closeness of log(S(a(n))) to gamma(n) is a property of the grid log(S(p)), not of the zeros. Proved: for every real t > log(3), if p is the first prime with log(S(p)) >= t and q is the prime preceding p, then 0 <= log(S(p)) - t < log(S(p)/S(q)) <= log(2), and log(S(p)/S(q)) = (1+o(1))*sqrt(t)*exp(-t/2). The upper bound log(2) follows from S(q) >= p, proved by induction from Bertrand's postulate; the asymptotic follows from the prime number theorem.
%C A397910 Terms a(1)-a(20) are certified: gamma(n) as a rigorous ball (Arb), exact prime sums computed with two different algorithms, and S(q) < exp(gamma(n)) <= S(a(n)) verified in interval arithmetic.
%H A397910 Antonio Mennillo, <a href="/A397910/b397910.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..20</a>
%H A397910 Antonio Mennillo, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18142838">Cumulative Prime Sums and Riemann Zeros: a fine grid, its ripple, and a family of prime races</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A397910 a(n) ~ sqrt(gamma(n))*exp(gamma(n)/2) (follows from the prime number theorem).
%e A397910 a(1) = 4691: gamma(1) = 14.1347251417..., exp(gamma(1)) = 1376046.57... The sum 1 + 2 + 3 + 5 + ... + 4679 = 1373345 is below it, while adding the next prime gives 1 + 2 + 3 + 5 + ... + 4691 = 1378036 >= exp(gamma(1)).
%o A397910 (Python)
%o A397910 from sympy import nextprime
%o A397910 from mpmath import mp, zetazero, exp
%o A397910 def a(n):  # fine for small n; certified computation of a(1)-a(20): see Links
%o A397910     mp.dps = 50
%o A397910     T = exp(zetazero(n).imag)
%o A397910     p, s = 1, 1
%o A397910     while s < T:
%o A397910         p = nextprime(p)
%o A397910         s += p
%o A397910     return p
%Y A397910 Cf. A002410, A007504, A397911.
%K A397910 nonn,hard,new
%O A397910 1,1
%A A397910 _Antonio Mennillo_, Oct 09 2026
